ga8H(){return"### Privacy Policy\n\n### 1. General Provisions\n\nThis Policy governs the data processing procedures in the \"OrderFlow\" application. The primary purpose of the application is to provide technical support for the order picking process.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Data Collection and Processing\n\n**2.1. Local Storage:** The application operates on an Offline-first principle. All operational data (order contents, picking statuses) is stored in a local database on the device and transmitted directly to the Company's server through secure communication channels (1C API).\n\n**2.2. Personal Data:** The application does not collect, store, or transmit personal employee data (such as personal messages, contacts, or media files) to third-party servers or cloud storage.\n\n**2.3. Use of System Resources:**\n\n- Camera access is requested solely for barcode scanning functions.\n- Notification access is used for timely receipt of information about new orders.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Confidentiality and Security\n\n**3.1.** The application Author does not have access to the Company's commercial information (product prices, customer data) passing through the application.\n\n**3.2.** All employee authorization data (personnel numbers, passwords) is processed within the Licensee's corporate network.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Policy Changes\n\nThe Author reserves the right to update this Privacy Policy to ensure compliance with application technical updates and applicable legislation."},
ga4M(){return"### License Agreement (EULA)\n\n### 1. Subject of the Agreement\n\nThis software \"OrderFlow\" (hereinafter \u2014 the Software) is a copyrighted work and intellectual property of the developer: **Dmytro Liashenko** (hereinafter \u2014 the Author).\n\nThe Licensee (Company) is granted a non-exclusive right to use the Software solely for automating internal order picking processes.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Intellectual Property\n\n**2.1.** This Software is not a work for hire. All exclusive proprietary and moral rights to the source code, database architecture (Drift/SQLite), unique synchronization algorithms, and graphical interface belong entirely to the Author.\n\n**2.2. The Licensee is prohibited from:**\n\n- Copying, modifying, decompiling (reverse engineering the code), or performing reverse engineering of the Software.\n- Transferring the rights to use the Software to third parties without written consent of the Author.\n- Using Software components to create proprietary software products.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Author's Rights and Limitations\n\n**3.1.** The Author has the right to display their name in the application and in all accompanying materials.\n\n**3.2.** Any modifications, enhancements, or customizations of the Software made by the Author at the Licensee's request automatically become part of the Author's intellectual property.\n\n**3.3.** The Author reserves the right to revoke the license in case of violation of the terms of use by the Licensee or non-payment of usage fees.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Warranties and Liability\n\nThe Software is provided \"as is\". The Author is not responsible for failures caused by incorrect configuration of the server side (1C API) or interference by the Licensee's staff with the application's engineering settings (Developer Mode)."},
